<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish Q4 current account surplus 454 mln punts-CSO.</title>
<headline>Irish Q4 current account surplus 454 mln punts-CSO.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ireland's current account surplus was a preliminary 454 million punts in the fourth quarter of 1996 versus a surplus of 299 million punts in the same quarter in 1995, Central Statistics Office figures showed on Thursday.  </p>
<p>The current account surplus for 1996 was 850 million punts compared with 1,070 million in 1995, the CSO said.  </p>
<p>				 1996 Q4	 1995 Q4</p>
<p>Current Account balance  454	     299</p>
<p>Merchandise		  2,211	   1,991</p>
<p>Invisibles		  -1,756	  -1,639</p>
<p>Cap and fin a/c balance  23	     -347</p>
<p>				 1996 year     1995 year</p>
<p>Current Account	    862	     1,072</p>
<p>Merchandise		  8,416	   7,459</p>
<p>Invisibles		  -7,554	  -6,390</p>
<p>Cap and fin a/c balance -1,241	  -934</p>
<p>(figures in millions of punts)</p>
<p>--Dublin newsroom +353-1-676-9775</p>
